# ExecuteAgentPlan.action - embodied_agent public high-level action for the
# Hermes natural-language flow. Endpoint name is fixed: /embodied/execute_agent_plan.
#
# See docs/lightweight_skill_package_registry_design_zh.md section 11.6.
#
# Reads the immutable plan by token, re-validates TTL, exact identity, task id
# and the task budget frozen by ConfirmAgentPlan, and re-runs the necessary
# Gateway / safety checks at action admission time.
#   1. A single step uses a direct root SkillCommand; workflow_digest is empty.
#   2. Two or more steps compute one typed workflow_digest and run Gateway
#      Begin / ordered child SkillCommand / Finalize. Hermes and robot-skill
#      never touch the root lease nonce.
#   3. First accepted execution of a token must carry an unconsumed
#      confirmation_token and bind the task id; retries with the same token /
#      task id may idempotently return the existing active/terminal record,
#      while a different task id returns SKILL_REQUEST_ID_CONFLICT. The
#      confirmation token admits exactly one new admission.
#   4. Action cancel must propagate to the current direct Skill or Workflow
#      child and wait for cleanup and the terminal result; receiving only
#      cancel accepted does not mean the robot has stopped.
#   5. On any step failure, cancel, timeout or unknown stop state, no further
#      step runs and no new token / task id is auto-created.
# robot-skill cancel-plan --task-id ID cancels this action's root goal via the
# standard CancelGoal interface. schema_version is 1 in v1.

# --- Goal ---
uint32 schema_version
string plan_token
string confirmation_token
string task_id
float32 timeout_sec
string trace_id
---
# --- Result ---
bool success
string plan_id
string plan_digest
string workflow_digest
uint32 completed_step_count
string error_code
string message
string actual_registry_epoch
uint64 actual_registry_generation
string actual_registry_digest
---
# --- Feedback ---
string state
string current_skill
uint32 workflow_step_index
string detail
